## Workflow feedback

The workflow agent owns this connection at stage entry/resume, each material
observation, and close-out. Read `hm intent status --json` through the launcher
below; load the task's SPEC/PLAN intent link and existing Feedback dispositions.
If status is not_filled_in, skip feedback; if invalid, report the error and do not
make a dependent intent decision. An absent intent layer costs no record or prompt.

1. Identify the relevant observation, source locator/time, affected question or
   metric ID, and task/intent link. For code-absent facts, use project-knowledge.
   If no PLAN exists yet, retain the evidence in the current SPEC/conversation and
   transfer it when execute creates the PLAN; never create a competing state store.
2. Reuse existing authorization only for the same operation and agreed scope.
   Follow the write rule below for unapproved mutations. If consent is pending or
   declined, write nothing and mark the update pending or declined. A question or
   proposal is not a recorded update. Never treat silence as consent or missing
   evidence as success. Do not ask again for the same confirmed operation.
3. After an authorized write, read back status; use that readback in the next decision.
   For missing, stale or conflicting evidence, diagnose within scope before the dependent decision.
   If the observation window is open, record its closing date and next eligible trigger; do not retry now.
   If uncertainty remains, ask the specific unresolved decision and continue only
   independent authorized work. A missed target is not automatically a new task.
4. On replay, link the existing disposition and follow-up; do not create duplicate work.
   Never rewrite terminal intent records; link delayed evidence to a consented new proposal.
   Distinguish completed task work from achieved intent outcomes. Measurements and
   their absence must inform the closure decision, not follow it.
5. Record the supported next decision and its authority. Continue agreed work only
   through the host's authorized stage/loop procedure. Goal/scope changes require
   the user. When no authorized work remains, record the stop reason and stop.
   If the host cannot invoke the next procedure, give an actionable handoff and
   explain the missing capability; never claim a stage ran from a suggested command.

Authoritative record map (link to these; do not copy their current state):

| Role | Record |
|---|---|
| Intent scope/lifecycle | `intent/<ID>.md` |
| Questions/metric definitions | `.claude/intent.yaml` |
| Measured values | `.claude/intent/metrics.yaml` |
| Domain facts | `.claude/memory/wiki.md` via project-knowledge |
| Criteria | `{{ config.spec.dir }}SPEC-<slug>.md` and its machine companion |
| Execution and disposition | `{{ config.work_docs.dir }}PLAN-<slug>.md`, Feedback section |

Use working links from SPEC/PLAN to the intent, relevant state IDs, source evidence
and prior/next task; preserve existing IDs, paths, history and approvals. The agent
records each disposition in the task PLAN's Feedback table:

| Evidence | Affected ID | Update status | Decision | Owner | Authority | Next action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| source path/anchor or conversation locator + time | intent/question/metric | recorded + readback / pending / declined / unchanged | supported action or stop reason | agent or user | consent/approved scope or pending decision | existing task link, specific question, dated deferral or stop |

## Real-task trial

At stage entry/resume, each material observation and closeout, resolve the base
project root and inspect `work-docs/PLAN-*.md` for an explicit trial activation.
If none is active, do nothing and ask no trial question. Do this even when the
intent layer is unfilled or the current task has no execution PLAN.

For each activated trial, use `hm intent --root <base> trial status <trial-id> --json`. Status separates observed candidates, committed members,
collection, outcome, source uncertainty and the next action; a read is never an
assessment. Follow its action during this invocation:

- `reconcile` or `resume_recovery_and_readback`: call
  `hm intent --root <base> trial reconcile <trial-id> --json` once, then independently read
  status again. Any session may perform this mechanical update under the recorded
  active policy. It does not need a previous collector's acknowledgment or a new
  user confirmation. If a write reports `lock_busy`, retry at the next eligible
  stage trigger; do not wait longer than the command's bounded lock period.
- `request_bounded_source_review`, `collect_missing_evidence`, or
  `resolve_order_conflict` / `resolve_source_conflict`: identify the named source,
  current inventory, observed cutoff and candidate order. Keep independent
  authorized task work moving. A user accepted historical population is recorded
  through `hm intent --root <base> trial record-decision` with an explicit decision file and
  the current expected revision; do not infer acceptance from readable logs,
  silence or a model summary. A blocked recovery keeps its next-trigger record.
- `request_policy_decision`: leave the existing policy effective. Record only an
  explicit user approved policy replacement using `record-decision`, then read
  status and reconcile under the newly recorded authority. Do not ask again if
  the decision already exists. Revoked authority forbids mechanical writes.
- `request_user_assessment`: present the observed trace and ask the user to
  decide each task's continuity result. Persist the exact explicit answer with
  evidence references and expected revision, then read it back. Never derive a
  pass/fail from task success, stage completion or the agent's own judgment.
- `wait_until_window_closes`: retain the closing date and next eligible trigger;
  do not remeasure or create a new task just to fill the trial.

Write task evidence in the earliest existing RESEARCH, SPEC or PLAN artifact as
`trial_feedback` frontmatter events, retaining one stable event ID per fact when
that fact is linked or moved to a later artifact. A start claim cites the existing
ledger first start; an observation links its concrete source and decision; a
terminal event records the actual task closeout, including failure or abort.
Intermediate stage handoff is not terminal. When no artifact exists yet, carry
its source facts into the first existing stage artifact during this invocation;
do not create a competing store. At closeout, update the current task artifact
first, then reconcile/read back the activated trial once more. If source writing
fails, report it as an evidence gap and preserve the next-trigger obligation.

The trial PLAN's typed `trial` frontmatter is authoritative for activation,
policy, membership and explicit human decisions. Its original prose remains
historical provenance. A worktree copy is never the authoritative trial PLAN;
all trial commands resolve the base root. The approved next-three-real-tasks
cohort is chronological by first start, includes failures/aborts and excludes
administrative/synthetic work under its original policy. Never reset members,
close the intent or declare trial success from implementation checks.
